From 82a6592568139a1cc83213717be1357050021071 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 13:57:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] docs(handoff): HANDOFF.md - what is true, what is not
 done, and what will bite the next agent
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A handoff rather than a tour. Nine sections, written for an agent who has never
seen this repository and will otherwise rediscover the same four defects.

WHAT IT CARRIES THAT IS NOT WRITTEN DOWN ANYWHERE ELSE

  · The open items, in priority order, each with the reason it is open. The old
    domain first: 35 redirect failures, ecowoodshardwood.com answering HTTP 200
    off Apache/2.4.68, twenty-two of those URLs customer testimonials with real
    names. Everything for it is prepared and it needs one Vercel command that
    an agent cannot run.
  · The shop-price state as measured against the live database rather than read
    off the seed file: 17 rows at placeholder prices, a live checkout, and no
    completed shop order. Both exits, and an instruction not to choose.
  · That verify-all SKIPS 15 network scripts, and that those are the only ones
    that catch the class of failure this project has shipped four times —
    F-107, F-129, F-131, and the week /quote-check 404'd while every guard was
    green.
  · The delivery loop, with the trap named: a patch uploaded through the GitHub
    web UI is COMMITTED rather than applied, which has produced green test runs
    against code that never changed. The `grep -c` step exists to make that
    impossible and is explained rather than just listed.
  · The sandbox limits, stated as limits — npm 403, push/fetch 403, no route to
    ecowoods.ca — with the note that adding the repo to the session's sources
    removes the need for patch files entirely.
  · Section 8, the non-obvious ones, each of which cost hours: render tiles at
    true floor scale with seams drawn or the banding is invisible; crop-scoring
    functions reward burl figure so always look; "jsx": "preserve" silently
    kills component suites at collection time; a test that can only see one
    file goes stale without anybody noticing.

ON RULE 4, WHICH NEEDED A NUANCE

The owner's rule is that guards may only be WIDENED, and that rule stands. But
two commits in this series inverted an assertion, so the handoff says when that
is legitimate: a guard whose PREMISE has become false is not protected by the
rule, provided the replacement covers strictly more than what it replaced —
which both HANDOFF-01 and CRAWL-01 do. Loosening a live guard to get green is
still not allowed, and the document says so in the same breath.

Definition of done is five steps and includes reading the REMOTE rather than
the local tree, because a push that reports success and moves nothing is a
failure this project has seen.

